  "description": "The Makita Variable Speed Heat Gun (HG6031VK) is designed for industrial applications and is ideal for a wide range of applications including vehicle wrapping and tinting, stripping lacquer, paint and varnish, defrosting frozen pipes, loosening tiles and putty, re-melting adhesives, removing wax and de-waxing, bending plastic tubes and sheets, and more. The HG6031VK features precise temperature control with a variable temperature control dial (122° - 1, 22° F) and 9 numbered settings, as well as two airflow settings (7 and 14 CFM) so the user can adjust the heat and blower speed to the application. The HG6031VK has a compact design (only 1.5 lbs). With rubber pistol handle. For added convenience during nozzle changes (nozzles sold separately), the integrated rear mount supports the gun in the \"up\" position. Added features include an integrated holding notch (strap sold separately), overheat protection, and a 6.5-foot cord for maneuverability. The HG6031VK includes a toolbox.",
